        "Map the forces from the payload through the beam or strut, connections and bearings into the supporting machine. For a beam, include bending about both axes and torsion from an eccentric carriage. For a compression link, evaluate global buckling, local wall instability and load eccentricity as well as material strength. A high longitudinal tensile modulus does not resolve all of these limit states.",
        "Request direction-dependent properties for the proposed laminate rather than a single carbon-fibre modulus. A fibre grade describes a constituent; the cured profile also contains resin and reinforcement in other directions. Open sections can twist under loads that appear to be simple bending, and laminate architecture influences that response. The section model, restraint assumptions and allowable deflection should therefore appear in the review before a tool or prototype is ordered.",
